# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-guard tooling (Node)
#
# The lockfile and manifest ARE committed; the installed tree is not.
# `Scripts/bootstrap-tooling.sh` restores it with `npm ci`, which installs the
# exact resolved versions the lockfile names and fails rather than resolving
# anything new.
#
# Vendoring node_modules was tried and reverted. It puts third-party source
# into a repository that has been through a public-readiness audit, it makes
# every dependency bump a large unreviewable diff, and it lets a checkout drift
# from the lockfile without anything noticing. A lockfile plus `npm ci` is
# reproducible without any of that.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scripts/tooling/node_modules/

# Golden-failure artefacts. Written by flutter_test on a golden mismatch;
# never evidence, and never something to commit.
test/failures/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Visual exploration evidence — local by default, tracked by exception
#
# `GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/` is a working area. It holds rejected rounds,
# contact sheets, blind-QA plates, per-round tooling, and — in at least one
# directory — **third-party reference imagery that must never be published**.
# `WALKSCAPE_REFERENCE_SET/README.md` says so in its own header: "REFERENCE
# EVIDENCE ONLY — NOT CANON — NOT A PROJECT STRIDE ASSET / DO NOT COMMIT".
#
# That instruction was not enough on its own. A `git add -A` during Playable
# Phase 2 swept 929 untracked files from this tree into the history of a
# **public** repository, the reference set among them. Untracking them at the
# tip does not remove them from pushed commits; that needed a history rewrite.
# See `MISTAKES.md` M-08.
#
# So the default is inverted: nothing here is tracked unless it is named below.
# A rule beats a README, because the README was already right and was still not
# read by the command that mattered.
#
# What stays tracked, and why:
#
#   * PIXELLAB_STABILIZATION_01/out/  — the packaging SOURCES. `package-art.js`
#     reads item icons, the gather animation, the world map and the location
#     vignettes from here, so `--check` cannot pass without them.
#   * PIXELLAB_PROOF_02/out/character/traveler_south_64.png and
#     traveler_portrait_64.png — the sprite and portrait the same script reads.
#   * PHASE1_CARRIED_CORRECTIONS/     — the Phase 1 correction patch.
#   * SKILL_ICONS_OD04/               — the OD-04 round that failed blind QA.
#     Kept deliberately: a failed round with a written verdict is the evidence
#     the next round is built on.
#   * *.md                            — round records and specifications.
#
# To track something new here, add an exception rather than removing this rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/**
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/**/
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/**/*.md
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/PIXELLAB_STABILIZATION_01/out/**
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/PIXELLAB_PROOF_02/out/character/traveler_south_64.png
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/PIXELLAB_PROOF_02/out/character/traveler_portrait_64.png
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/PHASE1_CARRIED_CORRECTIONS/**
!GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/SKILL_ICONS_OD04/**

# Never, under any exception: third-party reference imagery.
GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/WALKSCAPE_REFERENCE_SET/*.jpg
GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/WALKSCAPE_REFERENCE_SET/*.jpeg
GAME_BIBLE/ART/exploration/WALKSCAPE_REFERENCE_SET/*.png
